From 69382f9227fa7147b11cfb3480ffd30860c299da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:41:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(kanban): quota _outstanding/_unhinted read
 stored episodes through local run ids

A stored quota_episode payload keeps the recording gateway's run ids while event rows and
task_runs use this replica's (t_01a1d060012b9cd1). Two readers still compared them raw after
PR #1541 fixed the release:

- _outstanding filtered event rows by run_id >= the payload's episode_id, so on a replica whose
  ids run ahead it also took in walls of earlier, released episodes. It now starts at this
  replica's first run of the episode (_episode_runs, factored out of episode(), bound at
  _local_run(state)).
- _unhinted looked the payload's run_id up in local task_runs, found nothing and anchored the
  backoff at time.time() on every read, so a disproved hint stored without backoff_until never
  expired. It maps the run through _local_run and, failing that, anchors at the wall's
  recording time.

Both reuse kanban_quota_episode_release._local_run (PR #1541); no second mapping.
